{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cice_shortwave",
  "description": "CICE delta-Eddington shortwave radiation (stage 2 of the EqESM project): compute_dEdd_3bd (icepack_shortwave.F90:1703-3013) and its per-layer solver solution_dEdd (F90:3022-3488), the 3-band radiation scheme of the CICE sea-ice column. The model is a transcription of the Fortran law: the dzk/frsnw layer geometry (F90:2132-2156, 2122-2125); the snow IOP interpolation against the SNICAR grain-radius tables (F90:2396-2424, icepack_shortwave_data.F90:116-232) and the snow mass extinction ks (F90:2422-2425); the per-layer tau/w0/g assembly over the snow-cover, bare-ice and pond branches including the bulk aerosol mixing (F90:2425-2547, 2562-2717, 2549-2557); the per-band ocean albedo (F90:2772-2775); the delta-Eddington layer solution with the 8-point Gauss-Legendre angular integration of the diffuse reflectivity/transmissivity and the fresnel (refraction) layer at the base of the surface scattering layer (solution_dEdd F90:3296-3406); the downward and upward layer-combination recurrences with the trmin activity cutoff (F90:3287, 3408-3466); the interface flux fractions dfdir/dfdif (F90:2804-2832); and the band-weighted accumulations avdr/avdf/aidr/aidf, fsfc/fint/fthru, the visible/NIR transmitted fluxes and the Sabs/Iabs/fthrul layer absorptions (F90:2834-2960). The surface type srftyp (0 = air/bare ice, 1 = snow, 2 = pond) is a scalar parameter; the pond branch is transcribed but untested (the instrumented run contains no pond rows - see README-cice-shortwave.md). The 8-point Gauss diffuse reflectivity is written as an explicit sum over the 8 abscissas rather than an esm integral: no ESD quadrature rule exists for a bare mu axis (integral reaches evaluation only when an EarthSciDiscretizations rewrite rule lowers it; probed on this branch). The Fortran's trmin guard skips the layer solution below the cutoff; here the full solution is computed and the outputs are masked with the same condition, which reproduces the Fortran bit-for-bit (the guard condition is a property of the full solution). All laws are imported by reference from ./cice_templates.esm; the numeric tuples are extracted from the stage-1 instrumentation dump stage1/dumps/cice/cice_dedd.csv by stage1/analysis/gen_cice_dedd_tests.py.",
  "license": "MIT"
 },
 "function_tables": {
  "snow_iop": {
   "description": "SNICAR snow inherent optical properties (Qs_tab extinction efficiency, ws_tab single-scattering albedo, gs_tab asymmetry parameter) vs grain radius rsnw_tab and spectral band (icepack_shortwave_data.F90:107-232; the Fortran arrays are (nspint_3bd, nmbrad_snw) with column-major reshape, so the per-row triplets are bands 1, 2, 3). Interpolated with clamped linear interpolation in r exactly as shortwave_search + the delr lerp of compute_dEdd_3bd F90:2400-2424; the band axis is integral so bilinear lookup at an integer band is exact.",
   "axes": [
    {
     "name": "r",
     "values": [5.0, 7.0, 10.0, 15.0, 20.0, 30.0, 40.0, 50.0, 65.0, 80.0, 100.0, 120.0, 140.0, 170.0, 200.0, 240.0, 290.0, 350.0, 420.0, 500.0, 570.0, 660.0, 760.0, 870.0, 1000.0, 1100.0, 1250.0, 1400.0, 1600.0, 1800.0, 2000.0, 2500.0],
     "units": "um"
    },
    {
     "name": "band",
     "values": [1, 2, 3]
    }
   ],
   "interpolation": "bilinear",
   "out_of_bounds": "clamp",
   "outputs": ["Qs", "ws", "gs"],
