      "id": "cice_shortwave_bare",
      "description": "Bare-ice category (same cell, ncat 1, srftyp 0): hs = 0 so the snow branch is inactive and the column is the sea-ice SSL/delta-layer/interior stack with the unconditional ice aerosol mixing and the ocean albedo; band 3 truncates at the interface below the sea-ice SSL. The pins cover the layer geometry (the snow-layer dzk values are identically zero and not pinned), frsnw, the mixed tau/w0/g at the delta layer (the SSL values are identically zero and not pinned), the delta-Eddington layer props at one active layer per band (band 3 at the last layer above the cutoff), the downward chain at the top and bottom of band 1 plus the first guarded interface of band 3 (expected 0), the upward chain at the top of the column, the dfdir/dfdif fractions, the scalar accumulations and the Iabs/fthrul layer absorptions. The snow IOPs Qs/ws_snw/gs_snw/ks_snw and Sabs are not pinned: the dump records zeros for srftyp = 0 rows and Sabs is identically zero for bare ice. Tolerances: rel 1e-9 on the interface quantities, rel 1e-12 elsewhere.",
